  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ee8cfcb8b3588954ea24c10457255924, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5e889505e0e0d2a4db129b0905352109, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 65fabefe77170f948ba6088e0e5a0f95, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6a0ec25b8a422c646b399ddcae7b2c62, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 437fe84d57fc7f64cad7d56e2a8c9a89, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0d5771525d0e1814ab6d369e7eb1c3ba, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8881ea521aa0c7a4f9ae441c637350e6, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: e8c2b8bd9bd8f9e428347c57e9710cd4, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 09027ef61068784478c1b32badf50904, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: e8c38c6593d87944187086e01dbfdb98, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 31becc0a3e7892e468b4ac4372db4882, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: caf77e0d1f468b64ab86183d4318a7f8, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 579c9253f6a5be6499ca8a1851d07f90, type: 3}
  endOfLessonPromptMessage: You have finished the lesson. Press repeat to repeat
    the lesson or press next to .
  letsQuizInstructionMessage: Identify the onset of the word by pressing the dots
    of that letter.
  completedMessage: Great job! You finished the lesson.
  repeatQuestionMessage: 
  endOfLessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: eaf9daeefa1d1e14fb457ef584bacd86, type: 3}
  lessonPages:
  - title: 
    lessonText: Welcome to Lesson Five. Today, we will learn about onset and rime
      using the short E sound.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1d840590305a28e4596fdacc9e65567f, type: 3}
  - title: 
    lessonText: Words are made of different parts. The beginning sound of a word
      is called the onset.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9ad3b53a41785ca4ba73b5a9e3b4aba4, type: 3}
  - title: 
    lessonText: 'The ending part, including the vowel and any sounds after it, is
      called the rime.

'
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 818599a40fa765f4dae7ff4bd8b971eb, type: 3}
  - title: 
    lessonText: 'We can chop these words into two chunks. The onset is the starting
      consonant sound. '
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7ffbee3265706e548a99dee357bc0a52, type: 3}
  - title: 
    lessonText: The rime is the vowel and everything after it.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 88fe25ea2dfd1c04d806a225ba232227, type: 3}
  - title: 
    lessonText: For example, in the word 'web', the /w/ is the onset, and /eb/ is
      the rime.
    lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
    lessonAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1a3ce3db25323b441984988be8eca172, type: 3}
  quizQuestions:
  - displayLabel: 'Question 1: Net'
    categoryLabel: 
    promptMessage: Listen to the word Net. What is the first sound you hear in Net?
      Write the letter that makes that sound.
    successMessage: That is correct!
    wrongMessage: 
    displayImage: {fileID: -3454904030082182837, guid: edcc295c2bab20c45b6e5ba6ad6529a8, type: 3}
    introAudio: {fileID: 0}
    instructionAudio: {fileID: 0}
    successAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fb64d8ba31f566348a8908c5f49c1f65, type: 3}
    targetWordAudio: {fileID: 0}
    onsetAudioPromptMessage: 'Listen closely to the word: Net. /Nnn/ - et. What is
      the starting sound you hear in Net? Submit the Braille letter for that sound.'
    onsetAudioPromptClip: {fileID: 0}
    correctOnsetBraillePattern: 100111
    supportMessage: 
    supportAudio: {fileID: 0}
